  "updates.title": "Updates",
  "updates.intro": "Track what shipped in AOE2 game viewer and scan the latest release notes from one page.",
  "updates.tocTitle": "Table of contents",
  "updates.toc.release270": "Version 2.7.0",
  "updates.release270.version": "Version 2.7.0",
  "updates.release270.heading": "Release 2.7.0",
  "updates.release270.date": "July 25, 2026",
  "updates.release270.summary": "This release expands the AOE2 Spy overlay for live team games with more player information.",
  "updates.release270.bodyHtml": "<section id=\"release-2-7-0-team-games\">\n  <h3>More player information in live team games</h3>\n  <p>In live team games, the AOE2 Spy overlay now shows each player's 1v1 Random Elo, Team Elo, and civilization team bonus.</p>\n</section>",
  "updates.toc.release261": "Version 2.6.1",
  "updates.release261.version": "Version 2.6.1",
  "updates.release261.heading": "Release 2.6.1",
  "updates.release261.date": "June 30, 2026",
  "updates.release261.summary": "This release adds AOE2 Spy for live game overlays and followup strategies.",
  "updates.release261.bodyHtml": "<section id=\"release-2-6-1-aoe2-spy\">\n  <h3>AOE2 Spy live overlay</h3>\n  <p>AOE2 Spy shows an opponent's Elo and past strategies directly in the live game overlay.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-2-6-1-followup-strategies\">\n  <h3>Followup strategies</h3>\n  <p>The app now adds followup strategies so you can see what players transition into after the opening.</p>\n</section>",
  "updates.toc.release251": "Version 2.5.1",
  "updates.release251.version": "Version 2.5.1",
  "updates.release251.heading": "Release 2.5.1",
  "updates.release251.date": "June 24, 2026",
  "updates.release251.summary": "This release adds strategy filters to Custom Search and Custom Follow, detects opening strategies, and makes game history refresh more robust.",
  "updates.release251.bodyHtml": "<section id=\"release-2-5-1-strategy-filters\">\n  <h3>Strategy filters for Custom Search and Custom Follow</h3>\n  <p>Custom Search and Custom Follow now include strategy filters, so you can find and follow games by opening plan.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-2-5-1-detect-strategies\">\n  <h3>Strategy detection</h3>\n  <p>The app can detect opening strategies for supported games and show them alongside the match.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-2-5-1-history-refresh\">\n  <h3>More robust game history refresh</h3>\n  <p>Game history refresh is more reliable when loading and updating recent matches.</p>\n</section>",
  "updates.toc.release231": "Version 2.3.1",
  "updates.release231.version": "Version 2.3.1",
  "updates.release231.heading": "Release 2.3.1",
  "updates.release231.date": "June 11, 2026",
  "updates.release231.summary": "This release adds many more filters to Custom Search and Custom Follow, returns more follow results, and improves sharing and recorded-game playback.",
  "updates.release231.bodyHtml": "<section id=\"release-2-3-1-filters\">\n  <h3>More Custom Search and Custom Follow filters</h3>\n  <p>Custom Search and Custom Follow now include many more filters, so you can narrow games by more match settings.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-2-3-1-follow-results\">\n  <h3>More follow results</h3>\n  <p>Follow views return more matching games, giving you a deeper list to scan.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-2-3-1-sharing-playback\">\n  <h3>Sharing and recorded-game playback improvements</h3>\n  <p>Sharing is smoother, and recorded-game playback is more reliable when opening games from the app.</p>\n</section>",
  "updates.toc.release220": "Version 2.2.0",
  "updates.release220.version": "Version 2.2.0",
  "updates.release220.heading": "Release 2.2.0",
  "updates.release220.date": "June 6, 2026",
  "updates.release220.summary": "This release adds Recent Games links across follow cards, clickable player names, and local database results in Custom Search.",
  "updates.release220.bodyHtml": "<section id=\"release-2-2-0-recent-games\">\n  <h3>Recent Games links</h3>\n  <p>Follow cards now include Recent Games links so you can jump straight to a player's latest recorded matches.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-2-2-0-clickable-players\">\n  <h3>Clickable player names</h3>\n  <p>Player names in match lists can open that player's recent games.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-2-2-0-local-search\">\n  <h3>Local database results in Custom Search</h3>\n  <p>Custom Search can include local database results, making replay discovery faster and more complete.</p>\n</section>",
  "updates.toc.release210": "Version 2.1.0",
  "updates.release210.version": "Version 2.1.0",
  "updates.release210.heading": "Release 2.1.0",
  "updates.release210.date": "June 4, 2026",
  "updates.release210.summary": "This release adds custom follows and custom search for games by selected maps, players, or civs.",
  "updates.release210.bodyHtml": "<section id=\"release-2-1-0-follows\">\n  <h3>Custom follows</h3>\n  <p>Users can follow games of selected map, players, civs, or maps.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-2-1-0-search\">\n  <h3>Custom search</h3>\n  <p>Search games of selected map, players, civs, or maps.</p>\n</section>",
  "updates.toc.release200": "Version 2.0.0",
  "updates.release200.version": "Version 2.0.0",
  "updates.release200.heading": "Release 2.0.0",
  "updates.release200.date": "June 2, 2026",
  "updates.release200.summary": "This release adds Paste 'n Play, easier game sharing with friends, and a local save games manager.",
  "updates.release200.bodyHtml": "<section id=\"release-2-0-0-paste\">\n  <h3>Paste and play</h3>\n  <p>Paste a shared game link into the app and launch the replay directly, without manually hunting for the recorded-game file.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-2-0-0-share\">\n  <h3>Easy share games with friends</h3>\n  <p>Share a game link so friends can open the same match quickly from AOE2 game viewer.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-2-0-0-manager\">\n  <h3>Local save games manager</h3>\n  <p>Browse and manage local recorded games from one place when you want to replay, share, or clean up saved matches.</p>\n</section>",
  "updates.toc.release132": "Version 1.3.2",
  "updates.release132.version": "Version 1.3.2",
  "updates.release132.heading": "Release 1.3.2",
  "updates.release132.date": "May 29, 2026",
  "updates.release132.summary": "This release adds more ways to follow the games you care about, gives you control over local cache cleanup, and fixes a refresh bug that could break clicks.",
  "updates.release132.bodyHtml": "<section id=\"release-1-3-2-follows\">\n  <h3>Follow civilizations and maps</h3>\n  <p>You can now follow a favorite civilization or a map and open recent games for that civilization or on that map from the same workflow.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-1-3-2-purge\">\n  <h3>Purge cached games</h3>\n  <p>A new <strong>Purge</strong> button lets you delete locally cached games when you want to clear space or reset old replay data.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-1-3-2-favorites\">\n  <h3>Add to favorites</h3>\n  <p>You can now add supported items to your favorites so the views you revisit most stay one click away.</p>\n</section>\n<section id=\"release-1-3-2-refresh\">\n  <h3>Refresh click fix</h3>\n  <p>We fixed a page refresh bug that could invalidate clicks and make the page feel unresponsive after reloading.</p>\n</section>",
  "updates.backHome": "Back to home",
  "footer.privacy": "Privacy policy",
  "privacy.pageTitle": "AOE2 game viewer privacy policy",
  "privacy.eyebrow": "Privacy",
  "privacy.title": "Privacy policy",
  "privacy.updated": "Last updated: 2026-05-20",
  "privacy.intro": "This page explains what AOE2 game viewer stores locally, what it sends to our backend, and what may be shared with payment and public data providers when you use the app or website.",
  "privacy.backHome": "Back to home",
  "privacy.bodyHtml": "<section>\n  <h2>What this policy covers</h2>\n  <p>This policy applies to aoe2viewer.com, the AOE2 game viewer Windows app, and the support services behind them.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n  <h2>Website data</h2>\n  <p>The website is a static site. It stores your selected language in your browser local storage under <code>aoe2viewer.locale</code>. The site does not set its own analytics or advertising cookies in the current version. It also requests the public sponsor list from <code>api.aoe2viewer.com</code>.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n  <h2>Data stored on your device by the app</h2>\n  <p>The Windows app stores things such as followed players, selected player and view state, language override, and support prompt state on your device so the app can reopen the way you left it.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n  <h2>Data sent to our backend</h2>\n  <p>When the app detects a logged-in Steam account, it may sync your Steam ID, Steam display name, first and last login timestamps, followed players, and last-open view state to <code>api.aoe2viewer.com</code>. This is used to restore your setup across sessions and remember support status.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n  <h2>Support and payments</h2>\n  <p>When you open the support flow, the service may use your IP address and country to choose a payment provider and currency. If you complete a support purchase, we may store your Steam ID, Steam name, support amount, country, sponsor-list choice, order status, timestamps, and payment-confirmation payloads required to verify the payment.</p>\n  <p>FastSpring checkout sessions include an internal alias email based on your Steam ID together with your Steam name and sponsor-list choice. WeChat payment records may include your IP address and transaction IDs.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n  <h2>Public sponsor list</h2>\n  <p>If you opt in, your Steam name may be shown publicly on the sponsor list at aoe2viewer.com. If you do not opt in, your support is not added to that public list.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n  <h2>Public game and community sources</h2>\n  <p>The app uses public or community data sources such as Age of Empires stats, aoe2recs, AOE2 Companion, AOE Elo, and Liquipedia. When related features are used, those services may receive standard request data from your device or from the services that fetch data for the app.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n  <h2>How we use data</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Run replay, live spectate, language, update, and support features.</li>\n    <li>Sync followed players and last-open state for logged-in Steam users.</li>\n    <li>Process payments, verify sponsorships, and show public sponsors only when they opt in.</li>\n    <li>Protect the service and troubleshoot technical issues.</li>\n  </ul>\n</section>\n<section>\n  <h2>Sharing</h2>\n  <p>We do not sell your personal data. We share data only with service providers and public data sources needed to run the product, including Cloudflare hosting, FastSpring, WeChat Pay, the IP lookup service used for payment routing, and the public or community game data sources listed above.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n  <h2>Your choices</h2>\n  <p>You can browse the website without creating an account. You can clear the website language preference by removing site storage in your browser. In the app, you can leave the public sponsor option off if you do not want your name listed on the site.</p>\n</section>\n<section>\n  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>\n  <p>We may update this policy as the app changes. The page date shows the current version. For privacy questions or removal requests, contact us through the Discord or GitHub links on aoe2viewer.com.</p>\n</section>",
